      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242024",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/5d/5d1939b0e47c6bad6e08bb54be58e7f2c7ae22d2cfd2597e60430c207dc6683e.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $G$ is the point of intersection of the medians $AK^(\u2015)$ and $BL^(\u2015)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $AG: GK = 2: 1$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $BL^(\u2015)$ is a median of $\u25b3ABC$ | Given |\n| 2 | $L$ is the midpoint of $AC^(\u2015)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | $AK^(\u2015)$ is a median of $\u25b3ABC$ | Given |\n| 4 | $K$ is the midpoint of $BC^(\u2015)$ | Definition of a median |\n| 5 | $AB^(\u2015)\u2225LK^(\u2015)$ and $AB: LK = 2: 1$ | Midpoint theorem for triangles |\n| 6 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 7 | $\u2220BAG\u2245\u2220GKL$ | Alternate interior angles theorem |\n| 8 | $\u25b3ABG\u223c\u25b3KLG$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 9 | $AG: GK = 2: 1$ | CPSTP |"
    },
