      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-243056",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/70/7055a4c661444a7370de32e28d150d3f2ce7dd9b533702918923806eaaedb580.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $Q$ is the point of intersection of the medians $AM^(\u2015)$ and $BN^(\u2015)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $AQ: QM = 2: 1$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $AM^(\u2015)$ is a median of $\u25b3ABC$ | Given |\n| 2 | $BN^(\u2015)$ is a median of $\u25b3ABC$ | Given |\n| 3 | $M$ is the midpoint of $BC^(\u2015)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 4 | $N$ is the midpoint of $AC^(\u2015)$ | Definition of a median |\n| 5 | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| 6 | $\u2220BAQ\u2245\u2220QMN$ | Alternate interior angles theorem |\n| 7 | $\u2220AQB\u2245\u2220MQN$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 8 | $\u25b3ABQ\u223c\u25b3MNQ$ | AA similarity criterion |\n| 9 | $AQ: QM = 2: 1$ | CPSTP |"
